                <pb facs="0348" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00 Elections/101: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-16T12:00:00-05:00">October 16,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 11:04 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>220. Incomplete election returns indicate almost a clean sweep by the Cartelistes
                    or radical group largely controlled by Jolibois. This result came as a great
                    surprise to the mulatto Elite who are much disturbed. Reliably informed that the
                    Cartelistes state they will drive out of Haiti all those connected with the
                    Borno administration.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
